 "text": "9/29/26, 9:48 AM\nBusiness Context and Use\n\nThis inbound service operation receives a business partner\u2019s credit rating, calculated and sent by your credit management system,\nto your contract accounting system.\n\nRelated Operations\n\nThe Respond Credit Rating Query outbound service operation sends the requested information from the Credit Management\nprocess component.\n\nFeatures\n\nThe Respond Credit Rating Query inbound service operation provides the credit rating and the credit risk class for the requested\nparty.\n\nError Handling\n\nForward Error Handling\n\nThe Respond Credit Rating Query inbound service operation supports Forward Error Handling (FEH). The following error\ncategories are used:\n\ne DCE: Determination & Conversion Error\n\ne PRE: Processing Error\n\nFor more information about the individual error categories, see the code list for the global data type LogltemCategoryCode .\n\nMessage Types\n\ne FICA Rating Replicate Response\n\nNotes on SAP Implementation\nThe software component CA-SOA-ESM-ERP-FIN and business process CREDAGYOO]1 are used to support forward error handling.\nThe inbound proxy implementation updates the following data in the Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable:\n\ne Credit rating as sent from Credit Management (Table DFKKCRH)\ne Credit Management Master Data (Table DFKKCMS)\n\ne Trigger for a change to Contract Accounting after a change to Credit Management master data. (You use the trigger(s) in\nthe mass activity transaction FPBPCU).\n\nThe ValidityPeriod of the CreditRiskClass is not supported.\n\nEnhancements\n\nYou can use the FI-CA event 4602 to enhance the Credit Management master data. You can also use this event to enhance the Cl-\n",
